According to a new report from Intel Market Research, the global Quantum Dots Technology market was valued at USD 11 billion in 2025 and is projected to reach USD 50 billion by 2034, growing at a robust CAGR of approximately 17% during the forecast period (2025–2034). This growth is propelled by the expanding demand for high performance display panels, the rising adoption of quantum dot enhanced lighting, and the increasing interest of the biomedical sector in advanced fluorescent probes.
